The null check is unavoidable, so the only gain is to express it as a single conditional expression and hint the common non-null case, letting the compiler emit one compare plus a conditional move instead of a branch and two returns.

```cpp
FIT_UINT16 Mesg::GetNum() const
{
    return (__builtin_expect(profile != FIT_NULL, 1))
        ? profile->num
        : FIT_MESG_NUM_INVALID;
}
```